{
  "text": "A terminal is a lightweight web application with cryptographic capabilities. It chooses a chainpoint, retrieves data from a provider, and checks the evidence against a root from an anchor it accepts.\n\nThe provider supplies the data, but does not decide what the terminal should trust. A ledger proof can authenticate an output that contains an application root. The terminal can then use that root to verify an application proof.\n\nOnce the checks pass, the user can build a blockchain transaction, or use the verified information off-chain. Running your own anchor gives you independence over trust, while data providers compete on availability, capacity, and price.",
  "text_sha256": "3efba572a3ecfe6f2334aa89676a983f724af9cd23952bdee9c32e3c13b5c41e",
